# Where the outside pieces of the test rigs live on this machine. Copy this file to
# tests/rig.conf, which git ignores, and set what you have. One KEY=value per line, no quotes,
# no comments after a value; a leading ~/ is your home. Variables set in the environment win
# over the file. RIG_CONF=path (in the environment) reads another file instead.
#
# The emulator rigs (WinUAE, WarpOS, hosted AROS) are lrvne's: their keys (EMU, WINUAE,
# WINUAE_PPC, KICKSTART, WBDISK, WARPUP, BPPC_ROM, AROS_DIR, ...) are in
# lrvne/rigs/rig.conf.example; copy them into the same tests/rig.conf. Below are xenon's own.

# --- MorphOS in QEMU pegasos2 (tests/morphos/README.md) ---
#MOS_DIR=/path/to/morphos

# --- A real A1200 on the network (tests/amiga/README.md "The real A1200") ---
# Its address (telnetd on port 2323), a directory this machine's web server serves, and the
# URL under which the A1200 sees that directory.
#A1200=a1200.lan
#A1200_WWW=/var/www/html/xenon
#A1200_URL=http://this-host.lan/xenon
